        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Measure the storage space first, then buy the least mechanism
            that fits it.</strong> Under furniture wants a bare pad. A wardrobe or a car boot wants
            a double fold. A wall corner wants a single fold, or nothing at all.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Every hinge is deck length, money and long-term rigidity given away, so only buy one you
            will use. And once the format is settled, spend the attention on minimum speed, usable
            deck length and
            <a href="/walking-pad-with-incline/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">whether it inclines</a>
            — those decide how useful the machine is, while the fold only decides where it sleeps.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
